# Computer Vision using PyTorch

## Overview

This notebook provides a hands-on walkthrough of a **computer vision pipeline using PyTorch**. It walks through dataset preparation, model creation, training, evaluation, and visualization — all implemented in a clean, modular structure suitable for learning and reuse.

The focus is on **image classification** using convolutional neural networks (CNNs), and demonstrates end-to-end deep learning workflow in PyTorch. It is structured to support both educational use and real-world adaptation.

> This notebook runs entirely in Google Colab and is linked below.

## This project showcases:
- End-to-end **deep learning engineering** using PyTorch
- Clean application of **CNN-based classification**
- Use of `torchvision.datasets` and custom data loaders
- **Model training**, validation, and loss tracking
- Visual output of **predictions** and **evaluation metrics**

## Features
- Dataset preparation and normalization
- CNN model construction
- Training loop with loss/accuracy tracking
- Performance visualization with graphs
- Image prediction visualization (model outputs)

## Technologies
- Python
- PyTorch
- Torchvision
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab

